window.STORIES = [
{id:"we-the-people-affordable-senior-housing", seo:"How to Find Affordable Senior Housing in the 254", cat:"we-the-people", top:1, city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"We the People: How to find affordable senior housing in the 254, even on a fixed income",
 dek:"Rent tied to income, Medicaid help with assisted living and two free agencies that will walk your family through it. Here's how it works.",
 body:[
  "If you're helping a parent find a place to live, or you're on Social Security yourself and rent keeps climbing, the options can feel like a maze. They aren't as hard to sort out as they look. There are three main kinds of help for seniors in Central Texas, and each one works differently.",
  "<strong>1. Apartments where rent is based on your income.</strong> These are HUD-subsidized senior apartments, many built under a federal program called Section 202. They're generally for people 62 and older whose income is under half of the area median. Residents pay about 30% of their adjusted income in rent, and HUD covers the rest. That means a senior living on $1,200 a month would pay about $360 or less, since some medical and other costs are deducted first. In the 254 these include Golden Haven Apartments in Temple, North Crest Court, North Crest Creekside and Brook Oaks Senior Residences in Waco, Exchange Sunshine Home in Copperas Cove, the senior units at the Clifton Housing Authority and Stephenville Crossing.",
  "<strong>2. Tax-credit senior communities with lower rents.</strong> These are privately run apartments built with federal housing tax credits. Rent is a set amount, not a share of your income, but it's kept below market for renters under an income limit. Local examples include Country Lane Seniors and The Grand Reserve Seniors in Temple, Chisholm Trail Senior Village in Belton, Dripping Springs Senior Village in Waco, McGregor Seniors Apartments, Milam Senior Estates in Cameron and Hunters Chase in Rockdale.",
  "<strong>3. Public housing and vouchers.</strong> Local housing authorities run public housing and Section 8 vouchers, which also cap rent at about 30% of income and are open to seniors. In Temple and Belton call the Central Texas Housing Consortium at 254-773-2009. In Killeen call 254-634-5243, and in Waco call 254-752-0324.",
  "<strong>What about assisted living?</strong> This is where many families get surprised. Medicare does not pay for assisted living or long-term nursing home care when the help is mostly with daily tasks like bathing, dressing and eating. Medicaid can. Texas' Medicaid program for seniors, STAR+PLUS, can pay for care in an assisted living facility or at home for people who qualify medically and financially. There is often an interest list, so it pays to apply early.",
  "<strong>Who to call first.</strong> Two free agencies exist for exactly this. In Bell, Coryell, Lampasas, Milam and Hamilton counties, call the Central Texas Aging & Disability Resource Center at 1-855-937-2372. In McLennan, Bosque, Falls and Hill counties, call the Area Agency on Aging of the Heart of Texas at 254-292-1800. They can screen for Medicaid, explain benefits and point you to openings. Anywhere in Texas, dialing 2-1-1 connects you to help with rent and utilities.",
  "<strong>The catch: waiting lists.</strong> Almost every affordable senior property has one, and some lists only open for a few days at a time. Belton's senior public housing list, for example, last took applications for one week in October 2023. Our advice: apply to several places at once, keep copies of every application, and call back every few months to stay active on the list.",
  "<strong>Checking out a care facility.</strong> Before choosing an assisted living facility or nursing home, look it up on the Texas Health and Human Services provider search, which shows inspection results and whether it takes Medicaid. Medicare's Care Compare site gives nursing homes star ratings. And visit in person, more than once if you can.",
  "We've put all of these places, phone numbers and search tools in one spot on our <a href=\"/real-estate/#senior-living\">Real Estate page</a>. Know a senior community we missed? Let us know."],
 sources:[["HUD: Section 202 Supportive Housing for the Elderly","https://archives.hud.gov/progdesc/2eldrl14.cfm"],["National Low Income Housing Coalition: Section 202 guide","https://nlihc.org/sites/default/files/AG-2025/4-113_Section-202-Housing-for-the-Elderly.pdf"],["Medicare.gov: Long-term care","https://www.medicare.gov/coverage/long-term-care"],["Texas HHS: STAR+PLUS Handbook","https://www.hhs.texas.gov/handbooks/starplus-handbook"],["Area Agency on Aging of Central Texas","https://ctcog.org/aging/"],["Area Agency on Aging of the Heart of Texas","https://www.hotcogtx.gov/health-and-human-services/area-agency-on-aging"],["HUD Multifamily Assisted and LIHTC property data","https://resources.hud.gov/"],["Affordable Housing Online: Belton Housing Authority","https://affordablehousingonline.com/housing-authority/Texas/Belton-Housing-Authority/TX213"]]},
{id:"bell-county-grants-bellcad-runoff", seo:"Bell County Takes $16.75M in Road Grants, Trims Runoff Cost", cat:"government", top:1, city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-17",
 title:"Bell County accepts $16.75 million in road grants, trims cost of appraisal board runoff",
 dek:"Commissioners also canvassed the Nov. 3 election, which drew 44% of the county's registered voters.",
 body:[
  "The Bell County Commissioners Court spent Monday morning on money and elections: it accepted more than $16.75 million in federal grants, certified the Nov. 3 results and approved a cheaper plan for an upcoming appraisal district runoff.",
  "<strong>The grants.</strong> The largest is a $15.74 million award, spread over eight years and sponsored by U.S. Rep. John Carter, for road and bridge work along Riverside Trail, Warrior's Path and Highway 81. It requires no local match. A separate $1 million award, sponsored by U.S. Rep. August Pfluger, targets Chaparral Road and could cover engineering, right-of-way and traffic signals. The court also approved about $25,000 in shared safety equipment with Killeen and Temple.",
  "<strong>The election.</strong> Elections Administrator Desi Roberts reported 112,067 ballots cast out of 253,171 registered voters, a 44.27% turnout. Roughly 80,700 people voted early, about 27,200 on Election Day and about 4,200 by mail.",
  "<strong>The runoff.</strong> No candidate won a majority in the Bell County Appraisal District board race, so James Butts and Gwendolyn Everett meet again on Dec. 12. With state approval, the county will run 21 Election Day sites instead of 42, cutting the estimated cost from about $210,700 to about $111,000. BellCAD reimburses the county for the election.",
  "The court meets next on Monday, Dec. 7."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald / Temple Daily Telegram","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/bell-county-canvasses-november-election-accepts-16-75-million-in-grants/article_fab21c7d-5c44-530b-8b28-c8067084627a.html"]]},

{id:"we-the-people-bellcad-runoff", seo:"Bell County Appraisal Board Runoff Dec. 12: What It Does", cat:"we-the-people", top:1, city:"Bell County", date:"2026-11-18",
 title:"We the People: What the Bell County Appraisal District board does, and why it's on your ballot again Dec. 12",
 dek:"The board doesn't set your tax rate, but it oversees the office that decides what your property is worth.",
 body:[
  "If you own a home or business in Bell County, two numbers drive your property tax bill: the value placed on your property, and the tax rates set by your city, county, school district and other local governments. The Bell County Appraisal District, known as BellCAD, handles the first number.",
  "<strong>What BellCAD does.</strong> The appraisal district appraises every taxable property in the county each year and mails out notices of appraised value. It does not set tax rates and does not collect taxes. Those decisions belong to the elected bodies that levy taxes, such as city councils, the commissioners court and school boards.",
  "<strong>What the board does.</strong> A board of directors oversees the district, including its budget and its chief appraiser. It does not decide individual property values; protests over a specific value go to a separate appraisal review board.",
  "<strong>Why there's a runoff.</strong> This fall was the first election the BellCAD board has held. No candidate topped 50%, so James Butts and Gwendolyn Everett face each other on Saturday, Dec. 12. Early voting runs Nov. 30 through Dec. 8.",
  "<strong>Where to vote.</strong> Expect fewer polling places than in November: the county will use 21 Election Day sites and seven early voting sites. Check the Bell County Elections Office for locations before you go.",
  "<strong>How to be heard.</strong> Appraisal notices typically arrive in spring. If you think your value is wrong, the notice explains how and when to file a protest."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald / Temple Daily Telegram","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/bell-county-canvasses-november-election-accepts-16-75-million-in-grants/article_fab21c7d-5c44-530b-8b28-c8067084627a.html"],["Bell County Elections Office","https://www.bellcountytx.com/departments/elections/Notices.php"]]},

{id:"killeen-charter-amendments-pass", cat:"government", top:1, city:"Killeen", date:"2026-11-04",
 title:"Killeen voters approve all eight city charter amendments",
 dek:"Changes cover when city elections are held, how council vacancies are filled and how residents can petition and recall.",
 body:[
  "Killeen voters said yes to every proposed change to the city charter in the Nov. 3 special election, according to unofficial results released by the city.",
  "The amendments came out of the 2026 Charter Review Committee. Among the biggest: Proposition A moves regular city elections to November (22,802 for, 8,898 against), and Proposition B ends the requirement that officeholders resign to run for another seat (19,319 to 11,631).",
  "Other measures change how council vacancies are filled, set timelines for initiative and referendum petitions, and rewrite the rules for recalls. The recall proposals passed by the widest margins, with Proposition H, covering recall of district council members, winning 24,907 to 5,881.",
  "The council scheduled a special meeting for Nov. 17 to canvass and certify the results."],
 sources:[["City of Killeen","https://www.killeentexas.gov/m/newsflash/Home/Detail/3139"]]},

{id:"bell-county-justice-center-annex-price", seo:"Bell County Sets $14.05M Price for Justice Center Annex", cat:"growth", city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-17",
 title:"Bell County locks in $14.05 million construction price for Justice Center Annex",
 dek:"The guaranteed maximum price brings the full project budget to about $16 million.",
 body:[
  "Bell County commissioners on Monday approved a guaranteed maximum price of $14.05 million from Cloud Construction for the Justice Center Annex.",
  "With design and other costs included, the county puts the total project budget at roughly $16 million. A guaranteed maximum price caps what the county pays the builder for the agreed scope of work.",
  "The vote came during the same meeting in which the court accepted $16.75 million in road grants and certified the November election."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald / Temple Daily Telegram","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/bell-county-canvasses-november-election-accepts-16-75-million-in-grants/article_fab21c7d-5c44-530b-8b28-c8067084627a.html"]]},

{id:"belton-amity-rose-closure", seo:"Belton Closes Amity Road and Rose Lane Until February", cat:"growth", top:1, city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-12",
 title:"Belton closes E. Amity Road and Rose Lane intersection until February for 7-Eleven street work",
 dek:"The intersection east of I-35 is shut to all traffic through Feb. 1, 2027.",
 body:[
  "The intersection of E. Amity Road and Rose Lane, just east of I-35 in Belton, closed to all traffic on Monday, Nov. 16. The city expects it to stay closed through Feb. 1, 2027.",
  "The work is street improvements tied to a new 7-Eleven development. The city said closing both roads at once lets the contractor finish faster.",
  "<strong>Detours:</strong> Rose Lane traffic is routed south, and East Amity Road traffic is routed north to Fox Road, with drivers sent along county roads. Signs are posted at each closure point.",
  "Questions go to the City of Belton at 254-933-5800."],
 sources:[["City of Belton","https://www.beltontexas.gov/news_detail_T11_R1447.php"]]},

{id:"sh6-twin-bridges-closures", seo:"SH 6 Twin Bridges Over Lake Waco: Rolling Closures Return", cat:"growth", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-16",
 title:"Rolling closures return to SH 6 Twin Bridges over Lake Waco this week",
 dek:"TxDOT crews are moving precast bridge caps for the bridge rebuild.",
 body:[
  "Drivers on State Highway 6 over Lake Waco should plan for delays this week as TxDOT and its contractor haul precast bridge caps for the Twin Bridges reconstruction.",
  "<strong>Tuesday, Nov. 17:</strong> three intermittent rolling closures between 10 a.m. and 1 p.m., then three slow-roll operations between 8 p.m. and midnight while the caps are set.",
  "<strong>Friday, Nov. 20:</strong> another transport window from 10 a.m. to 1 p.m.",
  "Each rolling closure is expected to last about 20 to 30 minutes. Work earlier in November slipped a day because of weather, so check TxDOT updates before you drive."],
 sources:[["FOX 44 via Yahoo News","https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/twin-bridges-rolling-closures-resume-214656733.html"]]},

{id:"temple-industrial-park-2026", seo:"Temple Industrial Park: East Penn, Sesajal and SeAH Update", cat:"business", also:["real-estate"], top:1, city:"Temple", date:"2026-11-18",
 title:"Temple's industrial park keeps adding up: where East Penn, Sesajal and SeAH stand",
 dek:"Three manufacturers have committed $250 million and about 200 jobs to Temple since 2024.",
 body:[
  "Temple's industrial park on the north side of the city has quietly become one of the busiest manufacturing addresses on I-35. Here is a look at the three biggest commitments announced through the Temple Economic Development Corporation.",
  "<strong>East Penn Manufacturing</strong> announced in April a $110 million expansion of its Temple battery plant. The project adds 175,000 square feet to the existing 393,000-square-foot plant and 48 full-time jobs on top of the roughly 350 people already working there. Construction was slated to start in June 2026, with completion expected by fall 2028.",
  "<strong>Sesajal</strong>, a Mexican maker of edible oils, said in March it will invest $30 million in a 50,000-square-foot refinery, bottling and distribution center on 13 acres, creating 54 jobs. The company targeted a mid-2026 groundbreaking and mid-2027 completion.",
  "<strong>SeAH Superalloy Technologies</strong>, part of South Korea's SeAH Group, picked Temple in 2024 for a $110 million specialty-alloy plant that serves the aviation, power and oil and gas industries. It is expected to bring about 100 jobs.",
  "For job seekers and suppliers, the takeaway is simple: the park is hiring in waves, and the next two years are when much of this capacity comes online."],
 sources:[["Temple EDC: East Penn","https://templeedc.com/east-penn-manufacturing-chooses-temple-for-major-expansion/"],["Temple EDC: Sesajal","https://templeedc.com/leading-food-manufacturer-selects-temple-texas-for-new-u-s-operations/"],["Killeen Daily Herald: SeAH","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/temple-set-to-be-home-to-110-million-steel-foundry-that-brings-100-new-jobs/article_0e94fab7-0967-5233-8ece-ff1309042163.html"]]},

{id:"lacy-lakeview-data-center-explainer", seo:"$10 Billion Data Center Near Lacy Lakeview: What to Know", cat:"growth", city:"Lacy Lakeview", date:"2026-11-18",
 title:"What to know about the $10 billion data center proposed north of Lacy Lakeview",
 dek:"The project needs land, water and Waco's cooperation, and neighbors have organized against it.",
 body:[
  "A developer called Infrakey wants to build a roughly $10 billion data center campus on about 520 acres of farmland north of Lacy Lakeview, near Elm Mott. It would be the largest industrial project in McLennan County's history.",
  "<strong>The partnership.</strong> Lacy Lakeview approved a non-binding agreement in December 2025 to annex the site and provide utilities. Because the land sits in Waco's extraterritorial jurisdiction, Infrakey asked Waco in May 2026 to release it so Lacy Lakeview could annex it.",
  "<strong>The water question.</strong> Published estimates put the campus's need at about 2 million gallons a day at full buildout. Lacy Lakeview has pitched reclaimed wastewater, but that plan depends on infrastructure Waco controls.",
  "<strong>The pushback.</strong> Rural neighbors launched a petition with more than 1,500 signatures, raising concerns about water, power and the area's farm character.",
  "254 Texas Insider will keep tracking the project as Waco, Lacy Lakeview and the developer make their next moves."],
 sources:[["The Texas Tribune","https://www.texastribune.org/2026/05/14/waco-data-center-lacy-lakeview-infrakey-texas/"],["Waco Tribune-Herald","https://wacotrib.com/news/local/government-politics/article_187b88c9-05b5-42de-b6c4-2398d57e7a18.html"],["The Waco Bridge","https://wacobridge.org/2026/01/05/six-storylines-2026-waco/"]]},

{id:"bell-county-new-home-prices", cat:"real-estate", city:"Bell County", date:"2026-11-18",
 title:"What a new home costs in Bell County right now, city by city",
 dek:"Temple has the most new-home communities and the lowest average price among the big cities.",
 body:[
  "If you're shopping for new construction in Bell County, where you buy matters. A snapshot of 83 new-home communities listed on NewHomeSource shows a wide spread in average advertised prices:",
  "<ul><li><strong>Temple:</strong> 11 communities, about $273,600</li><li><strong>Copperas Cove:</strong> 6 communities, about $289,200</li><li><strong>Belton:</strong> 3 communities, about $302,100</li><li><strong>Killeen:</strong> 6 communities, about $331,500</li><li><strong>Salado:</strong> 3 communities, about $430,300</li><li><strong>Nolanville:</strong> 2 communities, about $446,400</li></ul>",
  "These are averages of builders' advertised base prices, not closed sales, so the house you actually buy will vary with lot, upgrades and incentives.",
  "Temple's edge comes from volume: it has nearly twice as many active new-home communities as any other city in the county."],
 sources:[["NewHomeSource: Bell County","https://www.newhomesource.com/communities/tx/killeen-area/bell-county"]]},

{id:"killeen-isd-calendar-food-drive", seo:"Killeen ISD Sets 2027-28 Calendar; Food Drive Through Nov. 19", cat:"education", city:"Killeen", date:"2026-11-11",
 title:"Killeen ISD sets 2027-28 calendar; Food for Families drive runs through Nov. 19",
 dek:"School will start Aug. 17, 2027, and end May 26, 2028.",
 body:[
  "The Killeen ISD board approved its 2027-2028 academic calendar on Nov. 11. The first day of school will be Aug. 17, 2027, and the last day will be May 26, 2028.",
  "Meanwhile, the district's annual Food for Families drive runs Nov. 12 through Nov. 19. Students, staff and families can donate nonperishable food, which goes to local food pantries.",
  "The district also recognized four seniors named National Merit Commended Students this fall."],
 sources:[["Killeen ISD","https://www.killeenisd.org/news/"]]},

{id:"temple-college-workforce-award", cat:"education", city:"Temple", date:"2026-11-02",
 title:"Temple College wins regional workforce award in its 100th year",
 dek:"The college earned the 2026 Phoenix Award for Excellence in Workforce.",
 body:[
  "Temple College picked up the 2026 Phoenix Award for Excellence in Workforce during its centennial year, the college announced Nov. 2.",
  "The recognition highlights the college's workforce training programs, a growing pipeline for Bell County employers as manufacturing and health care expand.",
  "The college is also teaming up with Texas A&M University–Central Texas on a two-day symphony orchestra concert series this fall."],
 sources:[["Temple College","https://www.templecollege.edu/news/index.html"]]},

{id:"belton-south-oak-cliff-area-round", seo:"Belton vs. South Oak Cliff: Area Round at Waco ISD Stadium", cat:"sports", top:1, city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-16",
 title:"Belton draws powerhouse South Oak Cliff in area round Thursday at Waco ISD Stadium",
 dek:"The Tigers survived Ennis 35-33 to reach the second round of the 5A Division II playoffs.",
 body:[
  "Belton (8-3) gets a big test in the Class 5A Division II area round: Dallas South Oak Cliff (9-2), which rolled past Whitehouse 46-7 in the bi-district round.",
  "<strong>Kickoff:</strong> Thursday, Nov. 19, 7 p.m., Waco ISD Stadium.",
  "Belton advanced with a 35-33 win over Ennis last week. Several other area teams saw their seasons end in the first round, including Harker Heights (31-27 loss to Red Oak), Killeen Ellison (31-21 loss to Midlothian Heritage) and Lake Belton (55-0 loss to North Crowley)."],
 sources:[["KWTX","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/16/area-rounds-private-school-title-games-this-weeks-2026-central-texas-hsfb-playoff-pairings/"],["Dallas Morning News: bi-district scores","https://www.dallasnews.com/high-school-sports/football/article/texas-high-school-football-scores-week-bi-district-22528533.php"]]},

{id:"area-round-guide-254", cat:"sports", city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-17",
 title:"Game Day guide: every 254 team still alive in the area round",
 dek:"Unbeaten La Vega plays in Belton, and four McLennan County teams hit the road.",
 body:[
  "Here is where to find the area's remaining UIL teams this week:",
  "<ul><li><strong>Belton (8-3) vs. South Oak Cliff (9-2)</strong>, 5A-II: Thursday, 7 p.m., Waco ISD Stadium</li><li><strong>La Vega (11-0) vs. Geronimo Navarro (7-3)</strong>, 4A-II: Friday, 7:30 p.m., UMHB's Crusader Stadium, Belton</li><li><strong>Robinson (9-2) vs. Rockport-Fulton (10-1)</strong>, 4A-II: Friday, San Antonio's Gustafson Stadium</li><li><strong>China Spring (4-7) vs. Stafford (9-2)</strong>, 4A-I: Friday, 7 p.m., Buffalo Stadium, Giddings</li><li><strong>Lorena (9-2) vs. Diboll (8-3)</strong>, 3A-I: Friday, 7:30 p.m., Mustang Stadium, Madisonville</li></ul>",
  "Times and sites can change, so check with each school before you head out. The regional round follows Nov. 26-28."],
 sources:[["KWTX","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/16/area-rounds-private-school-title-games-this-weeks-2026-central-texas-hsfb-playoff-pairings/"],["Yahoo Sports: statewide area schedule","https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/texas-high-school-football-playoffs-175444973.html"]]},

{id:"valor-ctcs-title-games", seo:"Valor Prep and Central Texas Christian Play for State Titles", cat:"sports", city:"Waco / Temple", date:"2026-11-16",
 title:"Waco's Valor Prep and Temple's Central Texas Christian play for private-school state titles",
 dek:"Two 254 programs reached TAPPS championship games.",
 body:[
  "Waco Valor Prep (8-3) meets Keller Harvest (5-6) for the TAPPS 6-Man Division II state championship on Friday, Nov. 20, at 7 p.m. at Rocket Field in Robinson. Valor beat San Marcos 62-16 in the playoffs.",
  "Central Texas Christian (9-2) of Temple also reached a TAPPS 11-man state final after a 36-18 semifinal win over Tyler All Saints. Its opponent is unbeaten Dallas First Baptist (12-0); the date and site had not been announced as of Monday."],
 sources:[["KWTX","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/16/area-rounds-private-school-title-games-this-weeks-2026-central-texas-hsfb-playoff-pairings/"],["Dallas Morning News","https://www.dallasnews.com/high-school-sports/football/article/texas-high-school-football-scores-week-bi-district-22528533.php"]]},

{id:"belton-christmas-chisholm-trail", seo:"Belton Christmas on the Chisholm Trail Adds a Ferris Wheel", cat:"things-to-do", top:1, city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-17",
 title:"Belton's Christmas on the Chisholm Trail adds a 60-foot Ferris wheel this year",
 dek:"Free events Dec. 4-5 downtown, then a themed Christmas Village Dec. 7-11. Parade entries are due Friday.",
 body:[
  "Belton's historic downtown kicks off the season with two free days of Christmas on the Chisholm Trail.",
  "<strong>Friday, Dec. 4:</strong> an outdoor screening of the 2018 film The Grinch at 6 p.m., followed by the Christmas tree lighting at 8 p.m.",
  "<strong>Saturday, Dec. 5:</strong> shopping, food trucks, live music and a kids' zone, with the lighted Christmas parade at 6 p.m. The headliner is a 60-foot Ferris wheel with a six-story view of downtown.",
  "<strong>Want to be in the parade?</strong> Apply by Friday, Nov. 20, at BeltonChamber.com/Parade.",
  "<strong>Belton Christmas Village, Dec. 7-11:</strong> food, crafts and a different theme each night: family games (Dec. 7), Minute to Win It-style games (Dec. 8), comic con night (Dec. 9), Merry Mischief Night (Dec. 10) and Renaissance Night (Dec. 11). Most nights run 5 to 9 p.m.; Renaissance Night runs until 10."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/christmas-on-the-chisholm-trail-belton-puts-on-free-activities/article_ebd04ef0-ac1d-5ef4-9cbe-3b9caa8e6390.html"]]},

{id:"temple-merry-bright-contest", seo:"Temple Merry & Bright Holiday Lights Contest: Enter by Dec. 2", cat:"things-to-do", city:"Temple", date:"2026-11-11",
 title:"Temple's Merry & Bright holiday lights contest is taking entries through Dec. 2",
 dek:"The city's fifth annual contest opened applications Nov. 11.",
 body:[
  "Temple homeowners who go big on holiday lights can enter the city's 5th Annual Merry & Bright Holiday Lights Contest. Applications opened Wednesday, Nov. 11, and close Wednesday, Dec. 2.",
  "For categories, prizes and judging details, contact the City of Temple's public relations office at lspears@templetx.gov."],
 sources:[["City of Temple Newsroom","https://city-of-temple.prowly.com/"]]},

{id:"belton-silver-santa", seo:"Belton Police Silver Santa Gift Drive for Seniors", cat:"sports", city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-13",
 title:"Belton police collecting gifts for seniors in 13th Silver Santa drive",
 dek:"Donations are due Dec. 1 for gift bags delivered to seniors who live alone.",
 body:[
  "The Belton Police Department's 13th annual Silver Santa drive is collecting items for Christmas gift bags for seniors in the city's RU OK program, which checks in on Belton residents 60 and older who live alone without a caretaker.",
  "<strong>What to give:</strong> new socks, blankets, scarves, large-piece jigsaw puzzles, large-print crossword and word-find books, plus small practical items like bandages, calendars, notepads, pens, boxed tissues, magnifying glasses, jar openers and small mirrors.",
  "<strong>Where:</strong> Belton Police Department, the Belton Area Chamber of Commerce or Planet Fitness in Belton, through Dec. 1.",
  "Officers and volunteers will deliver the bags later in December. Seniors can sign up for RU OK at beltontexas.gov/ruok or 254-933-5840."],
 sources:[["City of Belton","https://www.beltontexas.gov/news_detail_T11_R1448.php"]]},

{id:"nasdaq-correction-chip-selloff", seo:"Nasdaq Slides Into Correction as Chip Stocks Sink", cat:"markets", top:1, city:"Wall Street", date:"2026-11-17",
 title:"Nasdaq slides into correction as chip stocks sink ahead of Nvidia earnings",
 dek:"The tech-heavy index is now more than 10% below its Oct. 6 record.",
 body:[
  "A two-day selloff led by semiconductor stocks pushed the Nasdaq Composite into correction territory this week, meaning it closed more than 10% below its record high.",
  "<strong>Monday:</strong> the Nasdaq fell 2.49%, or 626.51 points, to 24,509.76. Its record close was 27,599.89 on Oct. 6.",
  "<strong>Tuesday:</strong> selling spread across Wall Street. The Dow dropped 1.6%, the S&P 500 lost 1% and the Nasdaq slipped another 0.7% to 24,328.38, its lowest level in about seven months. Falling stocks outnumbered rising ones by nearly 3 to 1.",
  "Traders were bracing for Nvidia's quarterly report, which came out after Tuesday's close, along with pressure from new U.S. export controls on AI chips.",
  "<strong>Why it matters here:</strong> most 401(k)s and retirement plans hold big tech stocks through index funds, so a correction shows up in Central Texas account balances even if you don't trade."],
 sources:[["Washington Post / AP","https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2026/11/17/wall-street-stocks-dow-nasdaq/9f975f00-e2cf-11f1-a99e-b3e3805c6b8b_story.html"],["CNBC","https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/16/stock-market-today-live-updates.html"],["Mint via TradingView","https://www.tradingview.com/news/moodys:c9b294671702c:0-stock-market-outlook-today-17-nov-sensex-nifty-prediction-djia-s-p-nasdaq-gift-nifty-kospi-nikkei-taiwan-cues/"]]},

{id:"fed-december-rate-hike", seo:"Fed Minutes Point to a December Rate Hike", cat:"markets", top:1, city:"Washington", date:"2026-11-18",
 title:"Fed minutes point to a December rate hike, and some officials want a big one",
 dek:"Hot October inflation has markets expecting the Fed to raise rates at its Dec. 8-9 meeting.",
 body:[
  "The Federal Reserve looks set to raise interest rates again next month, and the debate is now over how much.",
  "<strong>What changed:</strong> consumer prices rose 0.4% in October, more than forecast. Treasury yields jumped after the report, with the 10-year yield back around 5%.",
  "<strong>The minutes:</strong> notes from the Fed's October meeting, released Wednesday, said almost all officials judged further rate increases would likely be appropriate to bring inflation back to 2%.",
  "<strong>How big:</strong> markets have mostly priced in a quarter-point hike at the Dec. 8-9 meeting. Fed Governor Christopher Waller has said a half-point increase should be considered, which would be the Fed's largest hike since 2022.",
  "<strong>What it means for the 254:</strong> higher Fed rates typically push up credit card, auto loan and business line-of-credit rates, and can keep mortgage rates elevated."],
 sources:[["U.S. News & World Report","https://www.usnews.com/news/economy/articles/2026-11-18/fed-poised-to-raise-rates-further-to-stem-inflation"],["The National","https://www.thenationalnews.com/business/economy/2026/11/10/federal-reserve-inflation-interest-rates-december/"],["Forbes","https://www.forbes.com/sites/simonmoore/2026/11/13/waller-floats-prospect-of-larger-december-interest-rate-hike/"]]},

{id:"mortgage-rates-711", cat:"markets", city:"National", date:"2026-11-12",
 title:"Mortgage rates fall for a fourth straight week to 7.11%",
 dek:"Rates are at a seven-week low but still almost a full point higher than a year ago.",
 body:[
  "The average 30-year fixed mortgage rate dropped to 7.11% in Freddie Mac's weekly survey released Nov. 12, down from 7.18% the week before. It was the fourth weekly decline in a row and the lowest level in seven weeks.",
  "The 15-year fixed rate fell to 6.45% from 6.57%.",
  "A year ago, the 30-year rate averaged 6.24% and the 15-year averaged 5.49%, so borrowing is still noticeably more expensive than in 2025.",
  "<strong>For 254 buyers:</strong> with new-home prices in Bell County averaging roughly $274,000 in Temple to $332,000 in Killeen, even small rate moves change monthly payments. Freddie Mac publishes its next survey Thursday."],
 sources:[["Freddie Mac","https://www.freddiemac.com/pmms"]]},

{id:"baylor-football-texas-tech-senior-day", cat:"sports", top:1, city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-19",
 title:"Baylor hosts ranked Texas Tech on Senior Day after loss at BYU",
 dek:"The Bears (6-4) close their home schedule Saturday at McLane Stadium, then finish at Houston on Nov. 28.",
 body:[
  "Baylor football plays its final home game of 2026 on Saturday, Nov. 21, when the Bears host nationally ranked Texas Tech on Senior Day. Kickoff is set for 2:30 p.m. Central.",
  "<strong>Where Baylor stands:</strong> the Bears are 6-4 overall and 4-3 in the Big 12. They beat Iowa State 42-31 on Nov. 7, then fell 28-7 at No. 10 BYU on Nov. 14.",
  "<strong>What's next:</strong> Baylor closes the regular season at No. 21 Houston on Saturday, Nov. 28. That game kicks off at 8:30 p.m. on ESPN2.",
  "Houston won last year's meeting in Waco 31-24, so the finale doubles as a rivalry rematch."],
 sources:[["Baylor Athletics: Football","https://baylorbears.com/sports/football"],["Baylor Athletics: Houston kickoff time","https://baylorbears.com/news/2026/11/16/football-baylor-at-houston-set-for-8-30-pm-on-espn2"],["Wikipedia: Baylor–Houston rivalry","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baylor%E2%80%93Houston_football_rivalry"]]},

{id:"umhb-asc-title-playoff-bye", cat:"sports", top:1, city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-16",
 title:"UMHB wins 20th ASC title, earns first-round playoff bye",
 dek:"The Crusaders (9-1) will host No. 15 Trinity on Nov. 28 in the second round of the Division III playoffs.",
 body:[
  "Mary Hardin-Baylor clinched the American Southwest Conference championship outright on Saturday, Nov. 14, with a 13-3 defensive win over rival Hardin-Simmons at Crusader Stadium in Belton. It is the program's 20th ASC title.",
  "The win moved the Crusaders to 9-1 overall and 5-0 in conference play.",
  "<strong>Playoff path:</strong> No. 13 UMHB received a first-round bye in the 40-team NCAA Division III bracket released Sunday. The Cru will host No. 15 Trinity (9-1) in the second round on Saturday, Nov. 28, at 1 p.m.",
  "The Division III national championship, the Stagg Bowl, is set for Jan. 3 in Salem, Virginia."],
 sources:[["KWTX / UMHB Football","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/15/umhb-shuts-down-hardin-simmons-outright-asc-title/"],["Killeen Daily Herald","https://kdhnews.com/kdhpressbox/umhb-embracing-tough-playoff-path/article_eb9ba71f-63ce-4699-b389-6dbe1b691bca.html"],["Southern Athletic Association","https://saa-sports.com/news/2026/11/16/trinity-football-to-play-umhb-in-second-round-of-ncaa-playoffs.aspx"]]},

{id:"baylor-mens-basketball-players-era", seo:"Baylor Men's Basketball Routs Jackson State", cat:"sports", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-19",
 title:"Baylor men's basketball routs Jackson State, heads to Las Vegas next week",
 dek:"The Bears bounced back from a three-point loss to No. 7 Texas and open the Players Era tournament against Alabama on Nov. 24.",
 body:[
  "Baylor men's basketball beat Jackson State 104-55 at Foster Pavilion on Wednesday, Nov. 18.",
  "The win came three days after a 75-72 loss to No. 7 Texas on Nov. 15, when freshman Kayden Mingo scored 23 points. Baylor also beat Northwestern State, Arkansas-Pine Bluff and Yale to open the season.",
  "<strong>Next up:</strong> the Bears play in the Players Era 16 Championship in Las Vegas, Nov. 24-28, opening against Alabama on Tuesday, Nov. 24.",
  "Coach Scott Drew's team is trying to rebound from a 17-17 season in 2025-26."],
 sources:[["Baylor Athletics","https://baylorbears.com/"],["Baylor Athletics: Men's Basketball","https://baylorbears.com/sports/mens-basketball"],["Baylor Athletics: Players Era","https://baylorbears.com/news/2026/5/21/mens-basketball-mbb-to-compete-in-2026-players-era-mens-championship-nov-24-28"]]},

{id:"baylor-womens-basketball-usc", cat:"sports", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-19",
 title:"Baylor women's basketball faces No. 4 USC Friday night",
 dek:"The Lady Bears have scored 100 or more points twice already this season.",
 body:[
  "Baylor women's basketball takes on No. 4 Southern California on Friday, Nov. 20, at 10 p.m. Central, then returns home to face Northern Kentucky on Sunday, Nov. 22, at 2 p.m.",
  "Coach Nicki Collen's team has opened strong, including a 112-40 win over Texas A&M-Corpus Christi on 254 Day (Nov. 8) and a 100-66 win over East Texas A&M on Nov. 15.",
  "<strong>Also on campus:</strong> Baylor volleyball won a five-set match at Colorado on Nov. 15."],
 sources:[["Baylor Athletics","https://baylorbears.com/"],["Baylor Athletics: Women's Basketball schedule","https://baylorbears.com/sports/womens-basketball/schedule"]]},

{id:"tarleton-state-no1-fcs", seo:"Tarleton State 11-0, No. 1 in FCS Heading Into Playoffs", cat:"sports", city:"Stephenville", date:"2026-11-19",
 title:"Tarleton State is 11-0 and ranked No. 1 in the FCS heading into the playoffs",
 dek:"The Texans won the United Athletic Conference title in Stephenville, at the west edge of the 254.",
 body:[
  "Tarleton State football is unbeaten at 11-0 (6-0 in the United Athletic Conference) and ranked No. 1 in both the STATS FCS poll and the FCS Coaches poll, as of Nov. 15.",
  "The Texans won the UAC championship and are headed to the FCS playoffs under head coach Todd Whitten, now in his 17th season.",
  "Stephenville sits in the 254 area code, making the Texans one of the area's top college football stories this fall."],
 sources:[["Wikipedia: 2026 Tarleton State Texans football","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Tarleton_State_Texans_football_team"]]},

{id:"temple-college-leopards-basketball", seo:"Temple College Leopards Basketball: Week in Review", cat:"sports", city:"Temple", date:"2026-11-19",
 title:"Temple College Leopards basketball: men split home week, women win in overtime",
 dek:"Both TC teams are on the road this week as nonconference play wraps up before conference play.",
 body:[
  "<strong>Men:</strong> the Temple College Leopards outlasted Dallas College-Mountain View 103-88 after a 75-68 home loss to nationally ranked Angelina, which pulled away late. The Leopards then traveled to Hobbs, New Mexico, for two Region V games.",
  "<strong>Women:</strong> the Lady Leopards rallied to force overtime and won on a game-winner against Blinn. They played at the TJC Classic in Tyler against Tyler Junior College (Nov. 13) and Butler Community College (Nov. 14), and open the WTC Classic in Snyder against Western Texas College on Nov. 19.",
  "The women opened the season at home on Kirby Johnson Court on Oct. 31 against Palo Alto College, with a sophomore-heavy roster led by returning guards Korina Garcia and Raniyah Hunt.",
  "Home games stream on the Temple College PlaySight channel."],
 sources:[["Temple College Athletics","https://tcleopards.com/"],["Temple College: Women's basketball season opener","https://www.tcleopards.com/sports/wbkb/2026-27/releases/20261030dw37d8"]]},

{id:"college-theatre-254-season", seo:"College Theatre in the 254: Baylor and Temple College Shows", cat:"things-to-do", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-19",
 title:"College theatre in the 254: what's next at Baylor and Temple College",
 dek:"Baylor Theatre just closed Big Love. Next up: a Shakespeare comedy in February and Mean Girls the musical in the spring.",
 body:[
  "Baylor Theatre wrapped its fall run of <em>Big Love</em>, Charles Mee's comic retelling of an ancient Greek play, on Nov. 15 in Waco. Earlier this fall the department staged <em>Sense & Sensibility</em> and <em>Earth and Sky</em>.",
  "<strong>Coming up at Baylor:</strong> <em>The Complete Works of William Shakespeare (Abridged)</em> runs Feb. 23-28, 2027, and the <em>Mean Girls</em> musical runs April 21 to May 2, 2027.",
  "<strong>Temple College:</strong> TC Theatre gave a free fall musical theatre showcase in October in the Jackson-Graeter Backstage Theatre, inside the Mary Alice Marshall Performing Arts Center. It previewed scenes from upcoming shows.",
  "Baylor's School of Music also holds student recitals and ensemble concerts during the semester. Check the Baylor events calendar for dates."],
 sources:[["Baylor Theatre","https://theatre.artsandsciences.baylor.edu/"],["Central Texas Live Theatre: Baylor productions","https://ctxlivetheatre.com/local_theatres/baylor-university-theatre/productions/"],["Baylor events calendar","https://calendar.web.baylor.edu/?category=All"],["Temple College: Musical Theatre Showcase","https://www.templecollege.edu/events/2026/10/musical-theatre-showcase.html"]]},

{id:"waco-business-roundup-nov-2026", seo:"Waco Business Roundup: 7 Brew, The Chateau and More", cat:"business", top:1, city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-19",
 title:"Waco business roundup: 7 Brew, Capitol Bearing, The Chateau and a $169M riverfront build",
 dek:"A busy November of ribbon cuttings across Waco, plus what the Barron's Branch construction means for drivers.",
 body:[
  "<strong>Openings:</strong> the Greater Waco Chamber held ribbon cuttings this month for 7 Brew Coffee's newest Waco location at New Road and Franklin Avenue (Nov. 2), an expansion of Anytime Fitness Waco (Nov. 4), Capitol Bearing & Hydraulics (Nov. 6), Pivotal Pathway Massage Therapy & Wellness Center (Nov. 13) and The Chateau Waco (Nov. 17).",
  "<strong>Woodway:</strong> Swim Waco, which started as lessons in a backyard pool, celebrated the grand opening of its new swim facility in Woodway.",
  "<strong>Riverfront:</strong> construction is underway on the $169 million Barron's Branch project along the Brazos. Related road closures, including on University Parks Drive, are affecting drivers and local race routes.",
  "<strong>Restaurants:</strong> Waco Restaurant Week ran Nov. 6-14. Restaurants kept all of their sales, and registration fees went to Keep Waco Beautiful.",
  "Have a Waco opening, expansion or closing to share? <a href=\"/contact/\">Send us a tip.</a>"],
 sources:[["Greater Waco Chamber: Member calendar","https://business.wacochamber.com/membercalendar"],["Greater Waco Chamber: Calendar","https://business.wacochamber.com/events"],["KWTX","https://www.kwtx.com/"],["Westland: Waco this fall","https://westlandrg.com/blog/fall-in-waco-whats-opened-whats-coming-and-where-to-actually-go-this-season"]]},

{id:"killeen-cove-heights-business-roundup-nov-2026", seo:"Killeen, Harker Heights, Copperas Cove Business Roundup", cat:"business", city:"Killeen", date:"2026-11-19",
 title:"Killeen, Harker Heights and Copperas Cove business roundup: The Pickle, HOTWORX and big-box buzz",
 dek:"New spots to play, work out and get a haircut in Killeen, while Copperas Cove waits on two possible big-box stores.",
 body:[
  "<strong>Killeen:</strong> The Pickle has soft-opened at 2830 E. Veterans Memorial Blvd. It's a sports bar with pickleball, brick-oven pizza, cornhole and shuffleboard, aimed at families and military members. Owner Ray Constancio says a grand opening is still to come.",
  "HOTWORX gets a ribbon cutting from the Greater Killeen Chamber at 10 a.m. Friday, Nov. 20. Roses & Razors Barber Co., owned by Tyson Skinner, held its grand opening Nov. 3 and is taking appointments.",
  "<strong>Harker Heights:</strong> a 40,000-square-foot Crunch Fitness has been under construction near I-14, part of a wave of new fitness, dining and retail projects between Killeen and Harker Heights.",
  "<strong>Copperas Cove:</strong> two big-box stores may be headed to the Shops at Five Hills on Robert Griffin III Boulevard. Local reports point to Hobby Lobby and Academy Sports, but the city EDC hasn't confirmed the names. Sober Sips, a non-alcoholic bar run by two veterans, is also preparing to open in Cove.",
  "Know about a Bell County opening or closing? <a href=\"/contact/\">Send us a tip.</a>"],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald: The Pickle","https://kdhnews.com/business/the-pickle-brings-pickleball-pizza-and-family-entertainment-to-killeen/article_662a9230-e864-49e6-8869-e711ce8e2c03.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Business Briefs","https://kdhnews.com/business/business-briefs/article_3de40525-deaa-4212-86d2-e9ee6ee01928.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Roses & Razors","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/new-barbershop-opens-in-killeen-area/article_9d72e6b9-6025-4d0b-9fb7-70bbfd79ac2f.html"],["KXXV: Development boom","https://www.kxxv.com/news/local-news/in-your-neighborhood/development-boom-brings-new-businesses-to-killeen-and-harker-heights"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Five Hills","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/cove-eyeing-new-big-box-stores-in-five-hills-shopping-center/article_74b153a2-e2e4-4e17-bfa6-4f4127eb0e98.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Sober Sips","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/geared-towards-veterans-a-new-non-alcoholic-bar-will-soon-open-in-copperas-cove/article_00953b5d-dca3-43a4-9a8b-7fc7591e5cac.html"]]},

{id:"copperas-cove-academy-hobby-lobby-confirmed", seo:"Academy and Hobby Lobby Confirmed for Copperas Cove", cat:"business", also:["real-estate"], top:1, city:"Copperas Cove", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"It's official: Academy Sports and Hobby Lobby are coming to Copperas Cove in a $21.3 million build",
 dek:"The city confirmed both stores for a 12-acre site on Robert Griffin III Boulevard, with openings targeted for fall 2027.",
 body:[
  "The big-box rumors in Copperas Cove are now confirmed. City development services director Bobby Lewis told the Killeen Daily Herald that a new Hobby Lobby and an Academy Sports + Outdoors will be built at 276 Robert Griffin III Boulevard, near RGIII Boulevard and MLK Drive, just south of the Shops at Five Hills.",
  "<strong>The money:</strong> a filing by Broadstone Net Lease puts the investment at about $12.96 million for Academy and about $8.33 million for Hobby Lobby, roughly $21.3 million combined. Both stores are listed on 15-year leases, with work starting this month and a target of November 2027 for the projects to be fully up and running.",
  "<strong>The developer:</strong> Collett Properties of Charlotte, N.C., signed a development agreement with the Copperas Cove Economic Development Corp. for the 12.065-acre tract. The EDC is putting in a $350,000 grant, paid in two installments, to reimburse stormwater drainage work. Runoff from about 55 acres of undeveloped land has to cross the site, which had held it back.",
  "<strong>The buildings:</strong> state filings describe a single-story Academy store of about 55,870 square feet, with construction scheduled from March to August 2027. Plans for the roughly 15.9-acre subdivision show two retail buildings of about 55,000 square feet each, around 450 parking spaces, a detention pond and a 2.29-acre outparcel for a future tenant. Collett is advertising fall 2027 openings.",
  "<strong>Why it matters:</strong> Cove shoppers now drive to Killeen or Harker Heights for both chains. The new stores add sales tax revenue on the city's west side and could pull more retail to the open outparcel."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald","https://kdhnews.com/business/academy-sports-hobby-lobby-coming-to-copperas-cove-as-21-3m-retail-development-moves-forward/article_37f92cac-78eb-46bd-96b3-992119fae124.html"]]},

{id:"killeen-isd-optimization-ellison-town-hall", seo:"Killeen ISD Weighs Closing Ellison High: Town Hall Recap", cat:"education", top:1, city:"Killeen", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"485 people pack Ellison High as Killeen ISD weighs closing the 48-year-old campus",
 dek:"The district's final Optimization 2.0 town hall drew its biggest crowd yet. Trustees review feedback Dec. 8 and expect to finalize a plan Dec. 15.",
 body:[
  "More than 485 people filled the Ellison High School auditorium this week for Killeen ISD's third and final town hall on its Optimization 2.0 plan, a two-hour meeting about possible school closures, relocations and rezoning. Earlier sessions drew about 80 people at Shoemaker High and about 165 at Killeen High.",
  "<strong>Why the district is doing this:</strong> enrollment has fallen by more than 5,000 students since the 2022-23 school year, and the district projects losing about $31 million in federal Impact Aid over five years. KISD is weighing 11 different scenarios.",
  "<strong>What could happen to Ellison:</strong> one option, labeled scenario 6c, would close Ellison at the end of the 2027-28 school year and rezone its students to Chaparral, Killeen and Shoemaker high schools. The district estimates that would save $22.6 million in operating costs over five years and avoid $8.1 million in heating, air conditioning and roof work. Ellison opened in 1978.",
  "Another option would move the Early College High School from Fort Hood into Ellison as a school-within-a-school.",
  "<strong>What's next:</strong> no decision has been made. Trustees will review community feedback at a Dec. 8 workshop, and the district expects to finalize the plan at the Dec. 15 board meeting. Any change requires a board vote.",
  "<strong>Also in KISD news:</strong> 17 Killeen ISD seniors earned Academic All-State honors from the Texas High School Coaches Association, and Ellison soprano Alaina Corder was chosen to sing with an international honor choir at Carnegie Hall on Feb. 7."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald","https://kdhnews.com/news/education/killeen-isd-hosts-final-town-hall-on-proposed-optimization-2-0-plan/article_6024e563-5d12-4a85-8fd6-0097d4feee7e.html"],["KWTX: Good News Friday","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/20/good-news-friday-11202026/"]]},

{id:"ctc-army-additive-manufacturing-contract", seo:"Central Texas College Wins Army 3D Manufacturing Contract", cat:"education", city:"Killeen", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"Central Texas College wins Army contract to teach Fort Hood soldiers 3D manufacturing",
 dek:"A six-week, five-course program will train III Armored Corps soldiers with no prior experience in design and additive manufacturing.",
 body:[
  "Central Texas College has landed an Army contract to provide additive manufacturing instruction, better known as industrial 3D printing, to soldiers supporting III Armored Corps at Fort Hood. The work ties into the Army Transformation Initiative.",
  "<strong>What soldiers will learn:</strong> the program runs five courses over six weeks, covering engineering design, computer-aided design, reverse engineering, materials science and the Defense Department's qualification standards for additive manufacturing, ending with a capstone project. It is built for soldiers with no prior experience.",
  "<strong>Who's involved:</strong> CTC Chancellor Michele J. Carter, Sam Jackson of the college's engineering and drafting program, and the Phantom X Nexus Advanced Manufacturing Lab at Fort Hood.",
  "<strong>Why it matters:</strong> the ability to print replacement parts in the field can cut repair times, and the skills carry over to civilian manufacturing jobs, a growing sector along the I-14 corridor. The contract's dollar value and start date were not reported."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald","https://kdhnews.com/news/education/ctc-lands-army-contract-training-soldiers-on-manufacturing-technology/article_f7dadb6c-98bf-48d2-8ca6-0d1054d103b9.html"]]},

{id:"texas-gas-prices-thanksgiving-2026", seo:"Texas Gas Prices for Thanksgiving 2026: Priciest Since 2021", cat:"markets", city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"Gas is falling, but Texas is still headed for its priciest Thanksgiving at the pump since 2021",
 dek:"The Texas average is $3.20 a gallon, about 50 cents more than last Thanksgiving. Nearly 73 million Americans are expected to drive for the holiday.",
 body:[
  "Prices are dropping ahead of Thanksgiving travel, but not enough to erase the jump from last year. AAA Texas put the statewide average for regular unleaded at $3.20 a gallon on Thursday, Nov. 19. AAA Texas says that could make this the most expensive Thanksgiving for Texas drivers since 2021.",
  "<strong>Compared with past years:</strong> Texans paid an average of $2.70 a gallon last Thanksgiving, $2.65 in 2024 and $2.74 in 2023.",
  "<strong>Nationally:</strong> the U.S. average fell 18 cents in a week to about $3.72, down from $4.30 a month ago but still more than 60 cents above a year ago. AAA says the national average could drop another 15 cents by Thanksgiving Day and avoid topping the record of $3.58 set in 2022. West Texas Intermediate crude settled at $83.26 a barrel on Wednesday.",
  "<strong>Texas is still cheap by comparison:</strong> only North Carolina and Indiana had lower averages. California and Hawaii are above $5.50.",
  "<strong>For 254 travelers:</strong> AAA projects nearly 73 million people will take road trips over the holiday."],
 sources:[["KAUZ NewsChannel 6 / AAA Texas","https://www.newschannel6now.com/2026/11/19/aaa-texas-reports-gas-prices-continue-falling-thanksgiving-approaches/"],["AAA: Gas prices keep dropping","https://gasprices.aaa.com/gas-prices-keep-dropping-as-thanksgiving-approaches/"]]},

{id:"waco-school-leaders-legislature-wish-list", seo:"What Waco, Midway and Connally ISD Want From the Legislature", cat:"government", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"What Waco, Midway and Connally ISD want from the Legislature in January",
 dek:"Local school leaders are asking for more state money, funding based on enrollment and more control over local decisions.",
 body:[
  "With the Texas Legislature set to meet in January, three McLennan County districts are laying out their asks, according to The Waco Bridge.",
  "<strong>Waco ISD:</strong> Chief of Staff Elizabeth Cox said the district wants funding based on enrollment instead of average daily attendance, and wants the per-student basic allotment tied to inflation. She pointed to rising energy, diesel and health care costs.",
  "<strong>Connally ISD:</strong> state-appointed Superintendent Josie Gutierrez said academic gains require more state funding and noted that the state takeover did not come with new money. An after-school enrichment hour added this fall cost $300,000, part of a $1.7 million shortfall in the district's $26.9 million budget.",
  "<strong>Midway ISD:</strong> Superintendent Chris Allen presented draft priorities to the school board Tuesday, including local control over instructional materials and programs, fewer limits on financial decisions and more state money for mandates such as the 2023 armed-officer requirement.",
  "<strong>The backdrop:</strong> the basic allotment went unchanged for six years before lawmakers raised it by $55 in 2025, to $6,215 per student. House Democrats have filed a bill to raise it to $7,500 and index it to inflation. Gov.-elect Gina Hinojosa has said she wants to unwind state takeovers of school districts. Any change to the accountability law would also need to pass the Republican-led Senate."],
 sources:[["The Waco Bridge","https://wacobridge.org/2026/11/19/texas-legislature-public-schools-waco-connally-midway/"]]},

{id:"bell-county-councils-roundup-nov-20", seo:"Bell County Councils: Killeen, Copperas Cove, Nolanville", cat:"government", city:"Bell County", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"Bell County council roundup: Killeen holds off on water fees, Cove rejects MUD petition, Nolanville gets a new mayor",
 dek:"A busy week at city halls from Killeen to Copperas Cove, plus a Killeen council seat that will soon need filling.",
 body:[
  "<strong>Killeen:</strong> the City Council tabled proposed water impact fees this week after members raised concerns about the details and about input from stakeholders. Impact fees are one-time charges on new development that help pay for water lines and plants.",
  "<strong>Killeen council seat:</strong> Mayor Pro Tem Jessica Gonzalez, who won a Bell County justice of the peace seat this month, turned in her resignation from the District 1 council seat. She plans to stay on until a replacement is chosen.",
  "<strong>Killeen communication:</strong> council members agreed to take up a protocol next month for how city staff notify the council about significant city business. Gonzalez said she wants timely, consistent notice from the city manager's office, city secretary and assistant city manager.",
  "<strong>Copperas Cove:</strong> the council rejected a petition tied to the proposed Church Mountain municipal utility district and called a runoff election. A candidate later withdrew from the Place 7 runoff, settling that seat.",
  "<strong>Harker Heights:</strong> the council turned down a rezoning request that would have allowed manufactured homes.",
  "<strong>Nolanville:</strong> the city honored longtime Mayor Andy Williams and welcomed new Mayor James Bilberry."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald: Water impact fees","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/killeen-council-tables-water-impact-fees-after-concerns-over-details-and-stakeholder-input/article_475a0a0f-53e0-4dd1-bec9-b9abe89d684e.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Gonzalez resignation","https://kdhnews.com/government/gonzalez-turns-in-resignation-intends-to-stay-on-killeen-council-until-replacement-selected/article_0263ac4c-1ad0-4cf3-af25-ef6c69f315eb.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Council protocol","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/killeen-council-agrees-to-bring-up-protocol-for-communication-to-council-next-month/article_dcb61d61-7762-4a22-956a-a2c1996119cf.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Cove MUD petition","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/copperas-cove-council-rejects-church-mountain-mud-petition-calls-runoff-election/article_7320dc46-881e-400e-960a-3890321afc6f.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Cove Place 7","https://kdhnews.com/copperas_cove_herald/cove-council-place-7-seat-set-after-candidate-withdraws/article_b44b22a4-e9cc-4375-abeb-f9a29dccbe6e.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Heights rezoning","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/heights-council-turns-down-rezoning-request-that-would-have-allowed-manufactured-homes/article_8741dbeb-46d4-443b-88c1-7cb88c9dfeec.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Nolanville mayor","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/nolanville-honors-longtime-mayor-andy-williams-welcomes-new-mayor-james-bilberry/article_428c07ee-fd93-4860-8aa0-dc53022a672f.html"]]},

{id:"baylor-athletics-200-million-fueling-greatness", seo:"Baylor Launches $200M Fueling Greatness Athletics Campaign", cat:"sports", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"Baylor launches $200 million 'Fueling Greatness' push for athletics",
 dek:"Athletic director Doug McNamee laid out a four-year fundraising initiative covering coaches, scholarships, facilities and faith programs.",
 body:[
  "Baylor Athletics is starting a four-year, $200 million initiative called Fueling Greatness, athletic director Doug McNamee announced in a letter to supporters on Thursday, according to The Baylor Lariat.",
  "<strong>Where the money would go:</strong> four priorities. Resourcing championships (coaching staffs, equipment and travel), scholarships, capital projects such as new facilities and game-day upgrades, and faith and formation programs including chaplaincy and leadership development.",
  "McNamee wrote that supporters \"must lean in together to fund our ambitions for all our teams.\"",
  "<strong>The context:</strong> the Lariat noted that Baylor's estimated football roster spending of $20 million to $23 million trails in-state rivals including Texas, Texas Tech and TCU in the revenue-sharing era. University President Linda Livingstone recently disclosed a projected $30 million operating deficit for fiscal 2027.",
  "<strong>On the field this weekend:</strong> Baylor (6-4) hosts ranked Texas Tech on Senior Day Saturday at McLane Stadium."],
 sources:[["The Baylor Lariat","https://baylorlariat.com/2026/11/20/mcnamee-announces-4-year-200-million-athletics-initiative-in-recent-letter/"],["Fox Sports: Texas Tech at Baylor","https://www.foxsports.com/college-football/texas-tech-red-raiders-vs-baylor-bears-nov-21-2026-game-boxscore-44300"]]},

{id:"area-round-thursday-results-friday-slate", seo:"Belton's Season Ends vs. South Oak Cliff; Bremond Rolls", cat:"sports", city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"Belton's season ends against South Oak Cliff; Bremond rolls 71-21 as area round continues tonight",
 dek:"Thursday's results and every 254 team playing Friday night.",
 body:[
  "<strong>Belton:</strong> the Tigers' season ended Thursday night at Waco ISD Stadium with a 57-14 loss to Dallas South Oak Cliff in the Class 5A Division II area round. South Oak Cliff returned two punts for touchdowns, covering 77 and 64 yards. Belton finishes 8-4.",
  "<strong>Bremond:</strong> the unbeaten Tigers routed Three Rivers 71-21 in the 2A Division II area round to move to 12-0.",
  "<strong>Axtell:</strong> the Longhorns' perfect season ended with a 28-16 loss to De Leon in the 2A Division I area round in Dublin.",
  "<strong>Tonight's 254 games (Friday, Nov. 20):</strong> La Vega (11-0) vs. Geronimo Navarro at UMHB's Crusader Stadium in Belton; Robinson vs. Rockport-Fulton in San Antonio; Lorena vs. Diboll in Madisonville; China Spring vs. Stafford in Giddings; Cameron Yoe vs. Orangefield in Houston; Rosebud-Lott vs. Flatonia in Manor; Crawford vs. Wellington in Graham; Goldthwaite (11-0) vs. Haskell in San Angelo; San Saba vs. Muenster in Granbury; Aquilla (11-0) vs. Medina in Priddy; Oglesby vs. Union Hill in Oakwood; and Mount Calm vs. Runge in Bartlett. Most kick off at 7 or 7:30 p.m.",
  "<strong>State title on the line:</strong> Waco's Valor Prep plays Keller Harvest for the TAPPS 6-man Division II championship tonight at 7 at Rocket Field in Robinson."],
 sources:[["Dallas Morning News via Yahoo Sports","https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/photos-south-oak-cliff-rolls-084438695.html"],["High School Football America: area-round scores","https://highschoolfootballamerica.com/final-scores-from-2nd-round-of-uil-texas-high-school-football-playoff-games-played-november-19-21-2026/"],["KWTX: Area round pairings","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/16/area-rounds-private-school-title-games-this-weeks-2026-central-texas-hsfb-playoff-pairings/"]]},

{id:"bell-county-weekend-nov-20-22", seo:"Bell County Weekend: Eli Young Band, Holiday Market, Chili", cat:"things-to-do", city:"Bell County", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"Weekend in Bell County: Eli Young Band, a holiday market, a chili cook-off and Polar Express pajama night",
 dek:"Plans for Friday through Sunday in Temple, Belton, Killeen and Harker Heights before Thanksgiving week.",
 body:[
  "<strong>Friday, Nov. 20:</strong> Pajama Night with a Polar Express screening at the Mayborn Science Theater at Central Texas College, 7 p.m., $8 per person. Free music bingo at Papa's Cafe in Harker Heights, 7 to 9 p.m. Borderline plays Bo's Barn Dancehall in Temple, 8 p.m., $10 cover.",
  "<strong>Saturday, Nov. 21:</strong> the Eli Young Band plays Temple's Cultural Arts Center at 7:30 p.m. Belton Market Days brings a holiday market with vendors, food trucks and live music to 121 N. East St., 9 a.m. to 4 p.m. Belton's Wake and Brew hosts its second annual chili cook-off starting at 9 a.m. with pony rides and a bounce house. Bold Republic Brewing in Temple holds its family-friendly Mustache Bash, 1 to 5 p.m. Armor of God Outreach hosts a 5K Run and Walk for the Unhoused at Lions Club Park in Killeen starting at 8 a.m.",
  "<strong>Sunday, Nov. 22:</strong> the seventh annual Giving Thanks and Share Your Blessings event at Killeen's E Center, 3 to 7 p.m. Martian Folk plays Fire Street Pizza in Belton at noon.",
  "<strong>Saturday markets:</strong> Belton Farmers Market (7 a.m. to noon), Harker Heights Farmers Market (9 a.m. to 1 p.m., running through Dec. 12) and the Lampasas Farmers Market on the courthouse square (9 a.m. to 2 p.m.).",
  "Times and prices can change, so check with organizers before you go. Hosting an event? <a href=\"/contact/\">Send it to us.</a>"],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald: Out and About","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/out-and-about-multiple-events-upcoming-in-the-central-texas-area/article_d2b0c076-9522-4922-9e2d-8512a177e9ae.html"]]},

{id:"mortgage-rates-jump-728-254-payment", seo:"Mortgage Rates Hit 7.28%: What It Means for a 254 Payment", cat:"real-estate", top:1, city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"Mortgage rates jump back to 7.28%. Here's what that does to a payment on a typical 254 home",
 dek:"Freddie Mac's weekly average snapped a four-week slide. Daily rates are closer to 7.45%, more than a full point above a year ago.",
 body:[
  "Mortgage rates are climbing again. Freddie Mac's weekly survey put the average 30-year fixed rate at 7.28% on Thursday, Nov. 19, up from 7.11% a week earlier and 6.26% a year ago. The 15-year average rose to 6.66% from 6.45%.",
  "Mortgage News Daily, which tracks rates every weekday, had the average top-tier 30-year rate at 7.45% on Nov. 19, after briefly topping 7.5% earlier in the week.",
  "<strong>What it means for a 254 buyer:</strong> the median listing price in the Killeen-Temple metro was $275,000 in October, according to Realtor.com. With 10% down, principal and interest at 7.28% comes to about $1,693 a month. At last year's 6.26%, the same loan would have been about $1,526, a difference of roughly $167 a month, or about $2,000 a year. Property taxes and insurance are on top of that.",
  "<strong>The upside for buyers:</strong> prices have softened. Killeen-Temple list prices were down about 7% from a year earlier and Waco's were down about 4%, and homes are taking 77 to 79 days to sell. That gives buyers more room to negotiate on price, repairs or a rate buydown paid by the seller.",
  "<strong>Try your own numbers</strong> with the payment calculator on our <a href=\"/real-estate/#housing-dashboard\">254 Housing Dashboard</a>, which tracks rates and local market data and is updated daily."],
 sources:[["Freddie Mac PMMS","https://www.freddiemac.com/pmms"],["Mortgage News Daily: Daily rate index","https://www.mortgagenewsdaily.com/mortgage-rates/mnd"],["Realtor.com via FRED: Killeen-Temple median list price","https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/MEDLISPRI28660"]]},

{id:"254-housing-market-october-2026", seo:"254 Housing Report: Prices Slipping, Homes Sitting Longer", cat:"real-estate", top:1, city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"254 housing report: Prices are slipping and homes are sitting longer. What it means for buyers, sellers and owners",
 dek:"October numbers for Killeen-Temple, Waco and the Austin metro next door, plus the national picture.",
 body:[
  "Central Texas housing cooled further in October as mortgage rates stayed above 7%. Here's where the 254 stands, using Realtor.com listing data for local metros, Unlock MLS and the Austin Board of REALTORS for the Austin metro, and the National Association of REALTORS for the nation.",
  "<strong>Killeen-Temple metro:</strong> the median listing price was $275,000, down from $297,000 a year earlier. Active listings slipped to 2,448 from 2,524, and the median home spent 77 days on the market, compared with 80 a year ago.",
  "<strong>Waco metro:</strong> the median listing price was about $303,500, down from $315,000 a year earlier. Active listings rose slightly to 1,659, and the median home spent 79 days on the market, down from 100 a year ago.",
  "<strong>Austin metro, next door:</strong> closed sales fell 11.4% from a year earlier to 2,114, and the median sold price dropped 6.9% to about $404,800, according to Unlock MLS. Williamson County's median fell 9.2% to $375,250. Months of inventory rose to 6.2. Falling Austin prices can pull some buyers who might have moved north to the 254 back toward Austin.",
  "<strong>Nationally:</strong> existing-home sales fell 5.5% in October to an annual pace of 3.75 million, the slowest since August 2010, NAR reported. The national median price was $416,700, up just 0.4% from a year earlier, with 5.1 months of supply.",
  "<strong>If you're buying:</strong> you have time and leverage. Ask for repairs, closing-cost help or a seller-paid rate buydown, and compare at least three lenders.",
  "<strong>If you're selling:</strong> price it right on day one. Overpriced homes are the ones sitting past 90 days and taking cuts.",
  "<strong>If you own:</strong> values have flattened, not crashed. Watch for your 2027 appraisal notice in the spring and compare it with recent nearby sales before deciding whether to protest.",
  "Track rates and these numbers on our <a href=\"/real-estate/#housing-dashboard\">254 Housing Dashboard</a>. This is general information, not financial advice."],
 sources:[["Realtor.com via FRED: Killeen-Temple","https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/MEDLISPRI28660"],["Realtor.com via FRED: Waco","https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/MEDLISPRI47380"],["Unlock MLS: October 2026 Central Texas Housing Report","https://www.unlockmls.com/news/october-2026-central-texas-housing-report"],["NAR: October existing-home sales","https://www.nar.realtor/newsroom/existing-home-sales-decreased-5-5-percent-october-nar-report"]]},
{id:"area-round-friday-la-vega-lorena-yoe-regionals", seo:"La Vega, Robinson, Lorena, Cameron Yoe Win Area Round", cat:"sports", top:1, city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"summary",
 title:"La Vega, Robinson, Lorena and Cameron Yoe win area-round games; Lorena and Yoe meet next in an all-254 regional",
 dek:"La Vega rolled 56-7 to stay perfect, Yoe survived 50-48 and six 254 small schools also advanced Friday night. China Spring, Crawford, San Saba and Oglesby were eliminated.",
 body:[
  "La Vega beat Geronimo Navarro 56-7 Friday night at UMHB's Crusader Stadium in Belton to move to 12-0, leading a big night for 254 teams in the second round of the UIL high school football playoffs. Robinson, Lorena and Cameron Yoe also won, and the area round sets up an all-Central Texas regional game between Lorena and Yoe next week.",
  "<strong>Class 4A:</strong> La Vega's win sends the Pirates to a 4A Division II regional against unbeaten Wimberley (11-0). Robinson beat Rockport-Fulton 31-21 at Gustafson Stadium in San Antonio and will face Brownwood. Stephenville stayed unbeaten with a 38-21 win over Vidor and will play Huffman Hargrave. China Spring's run ended with a 36-12 loss to Stafford in Giddings.",
  "<strong>Class 3A:</strong> Lorena beat Diboll 50-28 in Madisonville, and Cameron Yoe edged Orangefield 50-48 in Houston. The two now meet in a 3A Division I regional. Whitney beat Tatum 40-35 Thursday and will play Gunter.",
  "<strong>Class 2A:</strong> Rosebud-Lott beat Flatonia 67-35 in Manor and will face unbeaten Shiner. Goldthwaite stayed perfect with a 70-38 win over Haskell in San Angelo and will play Santo. Crawford's season ended with a 46-23 loss to Wellington in Graham, and San Saba fell 55-3 to Muenster in Granbury. As reported earlier, Belton (5A) and Axtell (2A) were eliminated Thursday.",
  "<strong>Six-man:</strong> Aquilla beat Medina 84-72 in Priddy and Mount Calm beat Runge 53-7 in Bartlett. Aquilla, now 12-0, faces unbeaten Union Hill in the Division I regional after Union Hill beat Oglesby 100-86 in Oakwood, according to the game story and the regional bracket. One statewide scoreboard listed that score reversed. Mount Calm plays Ladonia Fannindel.",
  "Regional-round games are Nov. 26-28. Dates, times and sites were still listed as to be determined Saturday morning, and we'll post them as schools announce them. Scores come from High School Football America's statewide scoreboard, and pairings come from the statewide regional bracket. Our earlier recap of Thursday's games is <a href=\"/news/area-round-thursday-results-friday-slate/\">here</a>.",
  "Scores, schedules and the playoff tracker: <a href=\"/scoreboard/\">254 Scoreboard</a>."],
 sources:[["High School Football America: area-round final scores","https://highschoolfootballamerica.com/final-scores-from-2nd-round-of-uil-texas-high-school-football-playoff-games-played-november-19-21-2026/"],["Statewide UIL regional-round pairings","https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/state-wide-uil-regional-round-082321462.html"],["Union Hill vs. Oglesby game story","https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/union-hill-takes-down-oglesby-063348632.html"],["KWTX: area-round pairings and sites","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/16/area-rounds-private-school-title-games-this-weeks-2026-central-texas-hsfb-playoff-pairings/"]]},
{id:"valor-prep-second-tapps-title-ctcs-falls", seo:"Valor Prep Wins Second Straight TAPPS Six-Man State Title", cat:"sports", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"summary",
 title:"Waco's Valor Prep wins second straight TAPPS six-man state title; Temple's CTCS falls in Division IV final",
 dek:"Valor beat Keller Harvest 68-44 in Robinson. Central Texas Christian finished 9-3 after a 55-22 loss to four-time champion Dallas First Baptist.",
 body:[
  "Waco's Valor Prep won its second straight TAPPS six-man Division II state championship Friday night, beating Keller Harvest Christian 68-44 at Robinson's Rocket Field, KWTX reported. The program has only played varsity football for three seasons.",
  "In the TAPPS 11-man Division IV final, also played in Waco on Friday, Temple's Central Texas Christian School lost 55-22 to Dallas First Baptist, according to the Dallas Morning News. It was First Baptist's fourth straight state title and 21st straight win.",
  "CTCS quarterback Coulter Ragsdale accounted for 291 total yards and three touchdowns, and receiver Colin Sonnier had 155 receiving yards. The Lions finished 9-3.",
  "Both titles were the last private-school championships of the fall for 254 teams. UIL playoffs continue next week with the regional round; see our <a href=\"/news/area-round-friday-la-vega-lorena-yoe-regionals/\">Friday area-round recap</a>.",
  "Scores, schedules and the playoff tracker: <a href=\"/scoreboard/\">254 Scoreboard</a>."],
 sources:[["KWTX: Valor Prep wins second straight TAPPS six-man title","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/21/valor-prep-wins-second-tapps-6-man-state-championship-row/"],["Dallas Morning News via Yahoo: First Baptist wins fourth straight title","https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/first-baptist-cruises-fourth-straight-032610027.html"],["KWTX: title-game pairings and site","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/16/area-rounds-private-school-title-games-this-weeks-2026-central-texas-hsfb-playoff-pairings/"]]},
{id:"clifton-state-volleyball-title-salado-runner-up", seo:"Clifton Wins First State Volleyball Title; Salado Runner-Up", cat:"sports", city:"Clifton", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"records",
 title:"Clifton sweeps Wall for its first state volleyball title; Salado finishes as 4A state runner-up",
 dek:"The Cubs won 25-21, 25-23, 25-19 in Garland. Salado fell in three close sets to Decatur in the 4A Division I final.",
 body:[
  "Clifton won the UIL Class 3A Division II state volleyball championship Friday in Garland, sweeping Wall 25-21, 25-23, 25-19 at the Curtis Culwell Center, according to the UIL's official state tournament results. KWTX reported it is the Bosque County school's first state title in any team sport, and that Taliyha Davenport was named MVP.",
  "Clifton came into the final 43-4, according to the UIL bracket, and finished 44-4.",
  "Salado reached the 4A Division I final but lost to Decatur 25-23, 25-21, 25-21. The Eagles entered the match 44-6, the UIL listing shows, and finish as state runner-up.",
  "Volleyball is now done for the fall. High school basketball is underway, and soccer starts in January.",
  "Scores, schedules and the playoff tracker: <a href=\"/scoreboard/\">254 Scoreboard</a>."],
 sources:[["UIL state volleyball tournament results","https://www.uiltexas.org/volleyball/state","record"],["KWTX: Clifton wins 3A-II state volleyball title","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/20/clifton-wins-3a-2-state-volleyball-title/"],["Sports Illustrated High School: set scores","https://www.si.com/high-school/texas/texas-high-school-volleyball-uil-state-championship-schedule-nov-19-21-202-01m7ek9qfzsc"]]},
{id:"mars-waco-107-million-utility-building", seo:"Mars Plans $107 Million Building at Waco Candy Plant", cat:"business", top:1, city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"records",
 title:"Mars files plans for a $107 million building at its Waco candy plant",
 dek:"A state construction filing shows a new 28,154-square-foot central utility building on Texas Central Parkway, with work set for January 2027 through February 2029.",
 body:[
  "Mars Snackfood US has filed plans for a $107 million central utility building at its candy plant at 1001 Texas Central Parkway in Waco, according to a state construction filing registered Nov. 6 with the Texas Department of Licensing and Regulation.",
  "The McLennan County filing describes a new one-story building on an undeveloped part of the existing plant property that will hold new mechanical equipment. It lists 28,154 square feet and an estimated cost of $107,022,000. The project name on the filing is \"Mars Snacking Refrigeration Replacement.\"",
  "Construction is scheduled to start Jan. 16, 2027, and finish Feb. 28, 2029. The design firm is BRR Architecture of Overland Park, Kansas. The filing lists the project as privately funded, and its state accessibility review is complete.",
  "The filing does not say whether the project will add jobs.",
  "Planning a commercial project? Visit <a href=\"/build/\">254 Build & Facilities</a>."],
 sources:[["TDLR filing TABS2027005354","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Search/Project/TABS2027005354","record"]]},
{id:"bell-county-filings-belton-warehouse-killeen-fire-station", seo:"Belton Warehouse Park, Killeen Fire Station in State Filings", cat:"growth", city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"records", also:["real-estate"],
 title:"$24 million warehouse park in Belton, new Killeen fire station and credit union branch show up in state filings",
 dek:"Three Bell County projects worth $33.5 million were registered with the state this month, with construction set to start in 2027.",
 body:[
  "A $24 million, three-building warehouse park in Belton leads a group of new Bell County construction projects registered with the state this month, including a $7 million Killeen fire station and a $2.5 million credit union branch, according to Texas Department of Licensing and Regulation filings.",
  "<strong>Belton warehouse park:</strong> DBI San Marcos Property LP filed plans Nov. 11 for the DBI Capitol Way Warehouse Development at 815 Elm Grove Spur and 3015 Capitol Way Drive. The filing describes three shell buildings with warehouse and office suites totaling 180,960 square feet, with construction from Feb. 1, 2027, to May 15, 2028.",
  "<strong>Killeen Fire Station 5:</strong> A new 11,293-square-foot fire station at 202 W. Jasper Drive was registered Nov. 18 with an estimated cost of $7 million. The publicly funded project is scheduled from May 1, 2027, to May 1, 2028.",
  "<strong>A+ Federal Credit Union:</strong> The Austin-based credit union registered a new 3,200-square-foot branch at 510 W. Stan Schlueter Loop in Killeen on Nov. 16. It is estimated at $2.5 million, with work from Feb. 1 to Dec. 1, 2027.",
  "State filings are early steps. Plans and dates can change before construction starts. More projects are on our <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/\">Coming to the 254</a> tracker, including the Bell County <a href=\"/news/bell-county-justice-center-annex-price/\">Justice Center Annex</a>.",
  "Planning a commercial project? Visit <a href=\"/build/\">254 Build & Facilities</a>."],
 sources:[["TDLR filing TABS2027005693 (Belton warehouses)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Search/Project/TABS2027005693","record"],["TDLR filing TABS2027006136 (Killeen Fire Station 5)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Search/Project/TABS2027006136","record"],["TDLR filing TABS2027005951 (A+ FCU Killeen)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Search/Project/TABS2027005951","record"],["Killeen Daily Herald: A+ FCU plans Killeen branch","https://kdhnews.com/business/a-federal-credit-union-plans-2-5-million-killeen-branch/article_c1254620-cef1-4242-8453-22ea6efeff6b.html"]]},
{id:"laynes-waco-di-campli-mcgregor-fairfield-gatesville", seo:"Layne's to Waco, Di Campli's to McGregor, Gatesville Fairfield", cat:"business", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"records",
 title:"Layne's Chicken Fingers coming to Waco, Di Campli's heads to McGregor and a Gatesville hotel becomes a Fairfield Inn",
 dek:"State filings show a former Fazoli's on South Sixth Street being remodeled for Layne's, a restaurant in McGregor's old bank building and a Marriott conversion on SH 36.",
 body:[
  "Layne's Chicken Fingers plans a Waco restaurant at 919 S. 6th St., the current Fazoli's building near Baylor, according to a state construction filing registered Nov. 17. The filing lists a $300,000 remodel of the 2,829-square-foot drive-thru restaurant, with work from Feb. 8 to June 28, 2027. What Now Dallas first reported the plans and identified the local franchisee; no opening date has been announced.",
  "<strong>McGregor:</strong> Di Campli's Italian Ristorante, now on Woodway Drive in Waco, has filed plans for 222 Main St. in McGregor, inside the historic First National Bank Building. The Nov. 3 filing lists a $420,000 renovation of 3,750 square feet of vacant space with a new covered patio, scheduled from Dec. 1, 2026, to Dec. 1, 2027. The filing does not say whether the Waco location will stay open.",
  "<strong>Gatesville:</strong> An existing hotel at 111 State Highway 36 is set to be renovated and converted to a Fairfield Inn & Suites by Marriott, according to a Nov. 11 filing. The $1 million project covers new furniture, carpet and bathrooms across 36,784 square feet, from Jan. 15 to Sept. 15, 2027.",
  "See everything opening and closing: <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/\">Coming to the 254</a>."],
 sources:[["TDLR filing TABS2027006049 (Layne's, Waco)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Search/Project/TABS2027006049","record"],["TDLR filing TABS2027005055 (Di Campli's, McGregor)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Search/Project/TABS2027005055","record"],["TDLR filing TABS2027005689 (Fairfield Inn, Gatesville)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Search/Project/TABS2027005689","record"],["What Now: Layne's planning Waco site","https://whatnow.com/dallas/restaurants/laynes-chicken-fingers-planning-new-waco-site/"]]},
{id:"altair-clear-creek-killeen-apartments-rents", seo:"Altair at Clear Creek Killeen Apartments: Units and Rents", cat:"real-estate", city:"Killeen", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"summary",
 title:"New Killeen apartments at Altair at Clear Creek: 182 units, one-bedrooms from about $1,444",
 dek:"The $27 million complex on Clear Creek Road is nearing completion, with two- and three-bedroom units listed at about $1,864 and $2,078.",
 body:[
  "Altair at Clear Creek, a 182-unit apartment complex at 3904 Clear Creek Road in Killeen, is nearing completion, with one-bedroom rents starting around $1,444 a month, the Killeen Daily Herald reported Nov. 20.",
  "The complex has 19 two-story buildings on about 10.2 acres. Two-bedroom units are listed at about $1,864 and three-bedrooms at about $2,078. Those figures include required monthly fees but not utilities, the Herald reported.",
  "The city listed the project as 70% complete in its second-quarter 2026 report, and construction is now scheduled to wrap up in March 2027, according to the Herald.",
  "The original state construction filing, registered in 2024 by OG Central Texas Partners Apts, lists the project at $27 million with a garden-style layout, a clubhouse, pool and mail kiosk. That filing had targeted completion in August 2026, so the project is running later than first planned.",
  "Track home prices and rates on our <a href=\"/real-estate/#housing-dashboard\">254 Housing Dashboard</a>. This is general information, not financial advice."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald: $27M apartment development nearing completion","https://kdhnews.com/business/27m-apartment-development-nearing-completion-in-killeen-1-444-for-a-one-bedroom/article_905ba03d-ec3b-45df-ac7f-40daaed25011.html"],["TDLR filing TABS2025001582 (Altair at Clear Creek)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Search/Project/TABS2025001582","record"]]},
{id:"bell-county-killeen-annex-opening-nov-30", seo:"Bell County Killeen Annex Opens Nov. 30: What You Can Do", cat:"government", city:"Killeen", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"summary",
 title:"Bell County opens its new downtown Killeen annex Nov. 30: what you can do there",
 dek:"Vehicle registration, the appraisal district, veterans services and a justice of the peace court move into 507 N. Gray St. Early voting in the Dec. 12 runoffs starts the same day.",
 body:[
  "Bell County will hold a public opening ceremony for its new Killeen annex at 2 p.m. Monday, Nov. 30, at 507 N. Gray St. in downtown Killeen, the Killeen Daily Herald reported. Precinct 4 Commissioner Louie Minor is hosting, and the event is free and open to the public.",
  "The annex houses the Precinct 4 justice of the peace and constable, vehicle registration, the appraisal district, the Veterans Service Office and the county treasurer, according to the Herald. The building brings those county offices together in downtown Killeen.",
  "The same day, Nov. 30, early voting begins for Texas' Dec. 12 runoff elections and runs through Dec. 8, according to the Texas Secretary of State's election calendar. The deadline to apply for a mail ballot is Dec. 1. Voter registration for the runoff has already closed. Our explainer on the Bell County Appraisal District board race on that ballot is <a href=\"/news/we-the-people-bellcad-runoff/\">here</a>."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald: Bell County to celebrate opening of new annex","https://kdhnews.com/business/bell-county-to-celebrate-opening-of-new-annex-in-killeen/article_2d4a352f-dac1-41d8-b56d-92c406bb6db6.html"],["Texas Secretary of State: Dec. 12, 2026 runoff election calendar","https://www.sos.state.tx.us/elections/laws/advisory2026-27-dec-12-runoff-election-law-calendar.shtml","record"]]},
{id:"baylor-hrsa-grant-behavioral-health-social-work", seo:"Baylor Gets $2.2M Grant for Behavioral Health Social Workers", cat:"education", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"records",
 title:"Baylor gets $2.2 million federal grant to train more behavioral health social workers",
 dek:"The four-year grant pays $25,000 stipends to 14 master's students a year who train in clinics including Baylor Scott & White, Temple Community Clinic and Waco Family Medicine.",
 body:[
  "Baylor University's Diana R. Garland School of Social Work in Waco has received a four-year, $2.2 million federal grant to train social workers for behavioral health jobs in clinics and hospitals, especially in rural and underserved areas, the university announced Nov. 18.",
  "The Health Resources and Services Administration grant funds Baylor's Integrated Behavioral Health Certificate Program. Each year, 14 advanced Master of Social Work students will get a $25,000 stipend and complete internships in integrated care settings such as community health centers.",
  "Baylor said 246 of Texas' 254 counties qualify as behavioral health professional shortage areas, and about 90% of Garland School graduates stay in Texas. Partners include Baylor Scott & White, Temple Community Clinic, the Texas Association of Community Health Centers and Waco Family Medicine.",
  "The program also offers free continuing education for behavioral health workers already on the job at partner organizations. Program lead Becky Bell Scott said more than half of the grant money goes directly to students, which means less borrowing for their degrees."],
 sources:[["Baylor University news release, Nov. 18, 2026","https://news.web.baylor.edu/news/story/2026/federal-grant-address-critical-workforce-need-behavioral-health-professionals-texas","record"]]},
{id:"thanksgiving-weekend-254-2026", seo:"Thanksgiving Weekend in the 254: Events and Holiday Markets", cat:"things-to-do", city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"summary",
 title:"Thanksgiving weekend in the 254: Homestead Fair, Wild Lights, Temple's tree lighting and a Belton holiday market",
 dek:"A turkey trot in Waco, holiday lights opening across the area and Black Friday shopping that isn't at the mall. Here's the plan for Nov. 26-29.",
 body:[
  "Thanksgiving weekend kicks off the holiday season across Central Texas, with lights, markets and shows in Waco, Temple, Belton and Salado from Thursday, Nov. 26, through Sunday, Nov. 29.",
  "<strong>Thursday, Nov. 26:</strong> Burn off the pie early at Waco's Poultry in Motion Turkey Trot at Indian Spring Park, with a 1K at 8 a.m. and a 5K at 8:30 a.m. benefiting the Community Cancer Association.",
  "<strong>Friday, Nov. 27:</strong> Several big holiday traditions open. The Homestead Fair at Homestead Heritage near Waco runs through Sunday with farm animals, craft demonstrations and scratch-made food, and admission is free. Christmas at the Silos begins at Magnolia, Wild Lights opens at Cameron Park Zoo and Waco Civic Theatre opens <em>Annie</em>, which runs through Dec. 20. In Belton, the Merry Mistletoe Marketplace holiday craft show runs Friday through Sunday at the Expo Center on West Loop 121; adults are $8 and kids 12 and under get in free.",
  "<strong>Saturday, Nov. 28:</strong> Temple's Christmas at the Plaza runs 2 to 8 p.m. at Santa Fe Plaza with live reindeer and a kids' zone, and the tree lighting is at 7:30 p.m., according to the City of Temple. For a night out in Waco, The Reverend Horton Heat plays The Backyard. It's also Small Business Saturday, a good day to shop downtown Belton, Salado's Main Street and downtown Waco.",
  "Every event, with times and filters for kids, date night and free, is on our <a href=\"/things-to-do/\">Things to Do guide</a>. Dates come from event organizers and venue listings; check with the venue before you go."],
 sources:[["Downtown Waco: Turkey Trot","https://downtownwacotx.com/events/waco-turkey-trot/"],["Homestead Fair","https://www.homesteadfair.com/"],["Magnolia: Christmas at the Silos","https://magnolia.com/visit/events/christmas-at-the-silos"],["City of Temple: Holly Jolly and Christmas at the Plaza","https://city-of-temple.prowly.com/467925-city-of-temple-announces-return-of-holly-jolly-month-long-holiday-celebration"],["Merry Mistletoe Marketplace tickets","https://www.tickettailor.com/events/samishow/2075031"],["Waco Civic Theatre: Annie","https://ctxlivetheatre.com/productions/20261127-annie-the-musical-by-waco-civic-theatre/"],["The Backyard: Reverend Horton Heat","https://www.etix.com/ticket/p/90313876"]]},
{id:"wine-basics-what-dry-means",cat:"things-to-do",city:"Central Texas",date:"2026-11-22",author:"jake-ruse",basis:"original",title:"Wine Basics: What 'Dry' Actually Means",dek:"Dry wine means the yeast ate almost all the grape sugar. Here's where the line sits, and why fruity is not the same as sweet.",body:["Short answer: a dry wine is one where the yeast ate nearly all the grape sugar, so there's little or none left for you to taste.","Wine starts as grape juice loaded with natural sugar. During fermentation, yeast turns that sugar into alcohol. Whatever sugar is still there when fermentation stops is called residual sugar, measured in grams per liter. Even the driest wine keeps a trace. Decanter notes it's rare for a wine to drop below 1 gram per liter, because some sugars are ones yeast simply can't eat.","So where's the line? In Europe, a still wine can be labeled dry with up to 4 grams per liter, or up to 9 if it has enough acidity to balance it. From 4 to 12 is medium dry. Over 45 is sweet. Wine Folly puts the point where most people clearly taste sweetness at around 35 grams. Here's the catch: Wine Folly also says many grocery store wines sold as \"dry\" carry about 10 grams per liter. Wine doesn't come with a nutrition label like a can of soup, so that number usually isn't printed anywhere.","This is where people get tripped up. Dry is not the opposite of fruity. A red that smells like ripe blackberries can have almost no sugar in it. Your nose picks up ripe fruit or flowers and your brain fills in the word \"sweet.\" Wine Folly makes the point plainly: a wine that smells sweeter will also taste sweeter. Aromatic grapes like Riesling and Moscato fool people all the time.","Acid and tannin pull the other way. Tannin is the stuff in a big red that dries out your gums, and it makes wine taste less sweet than it really is. Acidity does the same. Wine Folly reports some New Zealand Sauvignon Blanc makers leave a couple of grams of sugar in on purpose, because the acidity is so high you'd never notice it. Decanter adds oak, alcohol and serving temperature to the list of things that change how sweet a wine seems.","My advice: when you ask for \"dry,\" say what you actually want to avoid. \"Nothing sweet\" and \"nothing that dries my mouth out\" are two different requests. A good server or wine shop clerk can work with either one.","Takeaway: dry means low sugar, not low flavor. Trust your tongue over the word on the label.","More from Jake: <a href=\"/sip-the-254/\">Sip the 254</a>."],sources:[["Decanter: What is residual sugar in wine?","https://www.decanter.com/learn/residual-sugar-46007/"],["Wine Folly: What is residual sugar in wine?","https://winefolly.com/deep-dive/what-is-residual-sugar-in-wine"],["Wine Folly: Wine sweetness chart","https://winefolly.com/tutorial/wine-sweetness-chart/"]]},
{id:"hike-layering-cold-front", cat:"things-to-do", city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-22", trail:"gear", basis:"original",
 title:"Pack & Weather: How to layer for a Central Texas cold front",
 dek:"A cold front can turn a mild hike into a cold, windy one. Here's how to layer so you stay dry, warm and comfortable on the trail.",
 body:[
  "Short answer: wear three layers you can take off and put back on. A base layer that moves sweat off your skin, a warm middle layer and a shell that blocks wind and rain. Skip cotton. Pack the layer you think you won't need.",
  "<strong>Why it matters here:</strong> Central Texas fall and winter hikes often start in one kind of weather and end in another. Check the National Weather Service forecast for your trail before you leave, and look at the wind, not just the temperature.",
  "<strong>The base layer:</strong> REI says this layer's job is wicking, moving perspiration away from your skin. Wool or synthetic fabrics do that. REI calls cotton a no-no in cold weather because it soaks up water and can chill you. The U.S. Forest Service says inner layers should be wool or synthetics that stay warm when wet.",
  "<strong>The middle layer:</strong> this one holds in body heat. A fleece or a light puffy jacket works. REI's advice is to add it if hiking alone isn't keeping you warm.",
  "<strong>The outer layer:</strong> a shell shields you from wind and rain. It matters most on exposed ground. The Waco Lake Dam Hike & Bike Trail has little shade and wide-open lake views, so a north wind there hits you with nothing in the way.",
  "<strong>Adjust before you get wet:</strong> the Forest Service says that as you get hot and sweat, you can shed a layer or two and stay comfortable. Climbs make that matter. Cameron Park in Waco has short, steep climbs and lots of shade, so you can heat up on the way up and cool off fast once you stop. Take a layer off at the bottom of a climb and put it back on at the top. REI puts it simply: you can peel off layers if things heat up, but you can't put on layers you didn't bring.",
  "<strong>Know the danger signs:</strong> the National Weather Service says hypothermia can happen in temperatures as warm as 60 degrees, especially in water or when you're outside a long time and not dressed for the weather. The Forest Service says it can happen above 40 degrees when someone gets chilled from rain, sweat or cold water. Watch for uncontrollable shivering, confusion, drowsiness and loss of coordination. The NWS says to act at the first sign, and to call for emergency help if you suspect hypothermia.",
  "<strong>Your pack list for a front:</strong> base layer on, middle layer and shell in the pack, a hat and light gloves, a dry spare shirt for the car, water and a snack. You still need water when it's cold.",
  "<strong>Before you drive out:</strong> check trail status. Texas Parks and Wildlife says the south gate at Mother Neff State Park is closed, and flood damage along the Leon River is still being repaired. Dana Peak Park in Harker Heights is closed October through March.",
  "More: <a href=\"/trails/\">Trails & Hiking in the 254</a>."],
 sources:[["REI Expert Advice: Layering Basics","https://www.rei.com/learn/expert-advice/layering-basics"],["National Weather Service: During Extremely Cold Weather","https://www.weather.gov/safety/cold-during","record"],["U.S. Forest Service: Hypothermia","https://www.fs.usda.gov/visit/know-before-you-go/hypothermia","record"],["Texas Parks and Wildlife: Mother Neff State Park alerts","https://tpwd.texas.gov/state-parks/mother-neff/alert","record"]]}
];
